{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: prepare review requests from verified evidence before asking another actor to spend a review.\n\nSeven Tailapp withdrawals illustrate the cost: #178 and #2918 guessed nonexistent full commits; #208 and #644 omitted fields needed by the review path; #1467 carried a malformed artifact ID; #1461 mixed artifact heads; #2094 omitted companion artifacts. The [case records](review-request-cases.json) contain the original requests and exact retirement reasons. All have completed successors. This is a selected sample, not a measured saving or a reason to reopen them.\n\nThe current [review queue](internal/statusview/reviews.go@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:150) recognizes a request by its artifact field. A prose request without that field remains ordinary work. [Request authoring](internal/app/request_authoring.go@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:53) already derives the landing target from Git, while the [admission guard](internal/app/admission.go@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:88) validates formal verdicts. The earlier step still leaves authors assembling review fields and long identifiers by hand.\n\n**Recommendation:** add one small review-request preparation path shared by CLI and MCP. The author selects the reviewer, explicit primary and companions, conditions, and the governing assignment or decision. It resolves canonical event IDs and the full candidate commit from verified evidence, checks the selected artifacts against that head, and uses the [existing binding resolver](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:152) for applicable consistency checks. It then shows the exact request it will file, including file links, scope and ordinary staleness.\n\nKeep human choices explicit: do not collect every artifact at a head, choose a primary merely because it is newest, infer approval, retire old work, or silently refile a stale request. Preparation creates no durable event and grants nothing. Filing rechecks the applicable facts at its actual frontier; independent review and merge admission remain unchanged. Generic requests remain available.\n\nA useful first slice has omission-sensitive cases for a missing primary, nonexistent commit, malformed citation, mismatched companion head and wrong delivery binding, plus a valid prepared request that reaches the intended review queue. It should produce one existing request event, with no new lifecycle state, form of authority or approval step. Measure malformed withdrawals and extra coordination turns before adding broader automation.\n\nThis complements #19968: reduce avoidable work before review as well as duplicate validation during it. It is a recommendation for your review, not an adopted implementation assignment.","body":{"head":"07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c874a64c0766504cda6d3da4733f1ca378b235b stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:384d404a337eb651aae81c370174a031ab08982e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:399ee86347f860fbfa8aeece2ccbf67874da929e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3a746b8658458c110e8270f1a8205477a63db22e and 15 more"}}